WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.840
The Rock is throwing stones.

00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:07.279
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson recently took to
Instagram to discuss the box office performance

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.160
of his latest flick, Hobbs &amp; Shaw.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.420
As of September 16th, 2019, the first-ever
spin-off film in the Fast and Furious franchise

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.980
has earned more than $740 million worldwide.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:22.280
Johnson posted a screenshot of a Deadline
article confirming Hobbs &amp; Shaw is currently

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:26.800
the best-earning non-superhero, non-Disney
movie of the year, but he also fired shots

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.720
at someone in the caption, which read:

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.800
"Assassins quietly play chess.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.560
Loud clowns play checkers.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.540
Thank you audiences worldwide for this incredible
support and massive win.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.840
Very cool and we're grateful for the love."

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.480
One of the hashtags the actor added was, quote,
"no candy asses", replacing the "e" with a

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:44.580
clown emoji.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.120
"Yeah, I thought it was a cool thing to say
in the moment."

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:49.420
So who's on the receiving end of his diss?

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.740
That would be none other than Tyrese Gibson,
a Fast and Furious franchise mainstay with

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.580
whom Johnson has been engaged in a drawn-out
and often dramatic feud.

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.940
Back when Hobbs &amp; Shaw was first starting
to take shape, Johnson was apparently faced

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:06.860
with a decision: go forward with that film,
or prioritize the ninth Fast and Furious movie,

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.920
originally slated to hit theaters on April
19th, 2019, according to The Hollywood Reporter.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:16.320
Ultimately, Johnson hopped on Hobbs &amp; Shaw,
and it wasn't long after the official announcement

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.060
dropped that Fast 9 was pushed back by almost
a year, moving to an April 10th, 2020 release

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.060
date.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:26.160
Johnson later noted that he wouldn't appear
in Fast and Furious 9 at all, according to

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:26.960
The Drive.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.180
It was an outcome that Gibson had desperately
hoped wouldn't happen.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:35.020
Gibson publicly begged Johnson not to move
ahead with Hobbs &amp; Shaw, writing in a since-deleted

00:01:35.020 --> 00:01:36.880
Instagram post, in part,

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:40.509
"If you move forward with that Hobbs movie,
you will have purposely ignored the heart

00:01:40.509 --> 00:01:42.160
to heart moment we had in my sprinter.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.540
I don't wanna hear from you until you remember
what we talked about...Fast family is just

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.540
that, a family.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:52.220
We don't fly solo...The Fast 9 release date
has already been announced and we can't let

00:01:52.229 --> 00:01:57.479
our loyal fans or our loyal Fast and Furious
fans down on any level from pushing the date...Didn't

00:01:57.480 --> 00:01:59.800
you see how HUGE [The Fate of the Furious]
was?

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.900
It's because we announced and KEPT our release
date bro."

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:07.380
After Johnson chose Hobbs &amp; Shaw and Fast
9 got delayed, tensions between Gibson and

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:09.080
Johnson continued to flare.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:13.300
"Alright, I've had enough of this s---."

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:18.680
Gibson blamed Johnson for the Fast 9 delay,
slamming him as greedy and self-centered in

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:21.049
an Instagram post that read, in part,

00:02:21.049 --> 00:02:26.309
"Congratulations to The Rock and your brother-in-law
aka 7 bucks producing partner for making the

00:02:26.309 --> 00:02:29.760
Fast and the Furious franchise about YOU...Fast
family, right?

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:30.300
Nah.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.040
It's about Team Dwayne."

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.819
Gibson later openly dissed Johnson again on
Instagram, accusing him of using steroids

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:40.290
and placing blame on the actor for making
the personal troubles he was dealing with

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.290
even worse.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:45.919
At the time, Gibson called Johnson a clown
and a, quote, "candy ass bitch", two things

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.060
Johnson referenced in his recent social media
post.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:54.460
In early August 2019, just a few days after
Hobbs &amp; Shaw opened in theaters on August

00:02:54.469 --> 00:02:58.930
2nd, Gibson posted a screenshot of a news
article that noted the film had posted the

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:04.099
lowest opening weekend for a Fast and Furious
franchise entry since the 2006 launch of The

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.240
Fast and the Furious: Tokyo Drift.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.680
The now-deleted post featured a caption that
read, in part,

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.559
"Breaking up the family clearly doesn't have
the value that one would assume it does…[Fast

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:19.400
Family] has more value as the [Fast Family]…180
million dollar global opening on Hobbs and

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.909
Shaw is NOT a win."

00:03:20.909 --> 00:03:25.099
At this point, it doesn't seem like the back-and-forth
bickering between Gibson and Johnson will

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.420
stop any time soon.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:30.200
With Johnson out of Fast and Furious 9, at
least the pair can avoid some potentially

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.280
painfully awkward days on set.

